  "title": "Erdős Problem #119",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $z_i$ be an infinite sequence of complex numbers such that $\\lvert z_i\\rvert=1$ for all $i\\geq 1$, and for $n\\geq 1$ let $ p_n(z)=\\prod_{i\\leq n} (z-z_i). $ Let $M_n=\\max_{\\lvert z\\rvert=1}\\lvert p_n(z)\\rvert$.\nIs it true that $\\limsup M_n=\\infty$?\nIs it true that there exists $c>0$ such that for infinitely many $n$ we have $M_n > n^c$?\nIs it true that there exists $c>0$ such that, for all large $n$, $ \\sum_{k\\leq n}M_k > n^{1+c}? $ ",
    "sha256": "4f6724ae2c6f011d3caa92b4ab87dd5a5e7fc8383d445178a61898549f84be26",
